WEBVTT

00:00:01.114 --> 00:00:12.992
Yes, I embraced tenderness and devotion
sou itooshisa to kizuna wo daita

00:00:13.126 --> 00:00:18.699
Floating in unending space
hatenaki umi ni ukabu

00:00:18.699 --> 00:00:25.628
On this small planet
chiisa na hoshi de

00:00:26.139 --> 00:00:37.175
When I feel your warmth next to me
anata no nukumori wo soba ni kanjiru toki

00:00:37.351 --> 00:00:43.290
I understand the burden
inochi no omosa to

00:00:43.290 --> 00:00:50.696
And the transience of life
hakanasa wo shiru no

00:00:53.467 --> 00:00:58.505
Nights of sorrowful wandering
mayoinageku yoru mo

00:00:58.505 --> 00:01:05.379
And tearful mornings
namida no asa mo

00:01:05.379 --> 00:01:10.984
I believe in tomorrow
ashita wo shinjiru kara

00:01:10.984 --> 00:01:17.257
So I can make it through
koeteyukeru no

00:01:17.257 --> 00:01:25.687
To the continuation of the dream
yume no tsuzuki he

00:01:35.108 --> 00:01:37.244
Why was Dumas there?

00:01:37.244 --> 00:01:40.304
Now that you mention it, he
hasn't been around for a while.

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:43.316
100 years ago he was
about 12 years old.

00:01:43.316 --> 00:01:45.051
And now he's about seventeen.

00:01:45.051 --> 00:01:47.554
That Orsel, you don't
think Dumas could have...

00:01:47.554 --> 00:01:50.614
It can't be! We discovered that technology.

00:01:50.857 --> 00:01:52.950
He couldn't have done it.

00:01:54.761 --> 00:01:56.062
It was Mel.

00:01:56.062 --> 00:01:57.757
Mel?

00:01:59.166 --> 00:02:02.727
Mel was captured by him
111 years ago.

00:02:03.670 --> 00:02:07.474
B-But Mel had already lost her memory!

00:02:07.474 --> 00:02:10.811
At that time, she didn't
even know who we were!

00:02:10.811 --> 00:02:12.479
That she was captured is a fact.

00:02:12.479 --> 00:02:15.812
And Dumas was at the scene
when the Orsel was released.

00:02:16.683 --> 00:02:18.385
What else could it be?

00:02:18.385 --> 00:02:20.376
That can't be!

00:02:21.288 --> 00:02:25.122
It's true that at that time
Mel had lost her memories.

00:02:25.392 --> 00:02:27.527
When we approach our twelfth year,

00:02:27.527 --> 00:02:29.796
our memories start to become distorted.

00:02:29.796 --> 00:02:32.458
We use our memory
records to reinforce them.

00:02:32.833 --> 00:02:34.768
After all the times we've experienced it,

00:02:34.768 --> 00:02:37.437
we estimated that we have
eleven years. But still...

00:02:37.437 --> 00:02:40.099
Exactly, we can't be certain.

00:02:40.841 --> 00:02:43.243
The few memories that Mel still retained,

00:02:43.243 --> 00:02:46.440
might have been cruelly
forced from her by Dumas.

00:02:50.650 --> 00:02:52.953
That old man named Kirchner,

00:02:52.953 --> 00:02:55.615
he said he was put on board a machine.

00:02:56.056 --> 00:02:58.425
Dumas must be using scientists here

00:02:58.425 --> 00:03:01.261
to develop a machine
that opens up the Zone.

00:03:01.261 --> 00:03:02.596
No, he's done it.

00:03:02.596 --> 00:03:04.030
Let's hurry!

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:08.268
Helga! We have to find
that girl before he does!

00:03:08.268 --> 00:03:09.803
Let's go to Kremer!

00:03:09.803 --> 00:03:11.738
Let's call Wonder, Aghi!

00:03:11.738 --> 00:03:13.365
Yes!

00:03:17.511 --> 00:03:19.206
She's here!

00:03:25.385 --> 00:03:26.943
Wonder!

00:03:28.221 --> 00:03:30.121
Wonder, the fog boats!

00:03:55.282 --> 00:03:57.147
Let's go, Wonder!

00:04:23.043 --> 00:04:27.946
THE GED GROUP

00:04:30.884 --> 00:04:32.752
I don't know...

00:04:32.752 --> 00:04:36.518
You usually need a government
permit to get on Ketplaque Island.

00:04:36.656 --> 00:04:40.592
I know that. We're just here to
inspect an old research lab.

00:04:40.694 --> 00:04:43.129
Come back for us in about an hour.

00:04:43.129 --> 00:04:44.998
I don't want to get into any trouble.

00:04:44.998 --> 00:04:47.228
One hour! One hour!

00:05:01.214 --> 00:05:04.274
This is the Phantom Ged research center?

00:05:06.152 --> 00:05:08.054
It would seem so.

00:05:08.054 --> 00:05:09.756
This is the place

00:05:09.756 --> 00:05:11.917
where that stone called the
Fragment was studied?

00:05:11.958 --> 00:05:14.828
According to the records,
Gherta became the director here

00:05:14.828 --> 00:05:17.353
when she was twenty-three.

00:05:17.731 --> 00:05:20.131
It's been almost thirty years since then.

00:05:20.333 --> 00:05:21.935
Even now it's supposedly

00:05:21.935 --> 00:05:24.995
an auxiliary facility of the Hague
University on the Eastern Mainland.

00:05:44.491 --> 00:05:47.727
W-Wait, Cooks! What if Gherta is here?

00:05:47.727 --> 00:05:50.163
Then we can question her directly.

00:05:50.163 --> 00:05:52.927
Unfortunately, it looks like she's out.

00:05:53.466 --> 00:05:57.960
Even so, I can't believe
there isn't even one guard.

00:06:11.618 --> 00:06:13.920
This is just a deserted building.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:15.689
Guess your hunch was off.

00:06:15.689 --> 00:06:18.491
I don't know what they studied here but

00:06:18.491 --> 00:06:20.894
it certainly doesn't look like a research lab

00:06:20.894 --> 00:06:22.759
of a secret government organization.

00:06:22.796 --> 00:06:24.423
Geez!

00:06:51.791 --> 00:06:55.562
Come on, let's go!
It's almost been an hour!

00:06:55.562 --> 00:06:57.587
Come look at this, Alice!

00:07:03.703 --> 00:07:05.538
A concrete passageway

00:07:05.538 --> 00:07:08.132
and a very thick, black steel door.

00:07:09.943 --> 00:07:11.570
What's that?

00:07:12.512 --> 00:07:16.642
An electric lock? The security's old.

00:07:19.853 --> 00:07:22.720
So, two are confirmed dead

00:07:22.756 --> 00:07:26.025
but the last one is missing, is that right?

00:07:26.025 --> 00:07:30.621
It's possible that he made his escape
amidst the confusion, correct?

00:07:30.864 --> 00:07:32.966
Perhaps the problem was
you underestimated him

00:07:32.966 --> 00:07:35.093
because you thought he was an old man?

00:07:35.335 --> 00:07:39.172
If this man wanders around and
tells people things he shouldn't,

00:07:39.172 --> 00:07:42.630
we won't be able to pass it off
as the story of a crazy old man.

00:07:43.143 --> 00:07:46.510
I'm going to use this man's
younger sister to lure him out.

00:07:46.646 --> 00:07:48.113
Kirchner is a man

00:07:48.148 --> 00:07:51.140
who escaped the rehabilitation
facility for his sister's sake.

00:07:51.351 --> 00:07:53.787
He'll definitely show up.

00:07:53.787 --> 00:07:56.415
Do you really think he'll fall for that?

00:07:56.623 --> 00:07:58.658
I am a scientist.

00:07:58.658 --> 00:08:00.819
The management of the
organization is your job!

00:08:00.860 --> 00:08:02.462
The current situation

00:08:02.462 --> 00:08:04.521
is also the result of an oversight
by the facilities management.

00:08:04.597 --> 00:08:08.434
Even so, you are the person
responsible for this whole experiment.

00:08:08.434 --> 00:08:11.304
We don't know anything about science.

00:08:11.304 --> 00:08:15.008
Shouldn't you have been able to
predict that the man named Kirchner

00:08:15.008 --> 00:08:17.272
would emit strange electricity like that?

00:08:17.343 --> 00:08:20.446
No human being can do that.

00:08:20.446 --> 00:08:22.215
He's nothing more than a monster.

00:08:22.215 --> 00:08:24.584
Is that why you ordered him killed?

00:08:24.584 --> 00:08:27.821
These people are not guinea pigs!
They're human beings!

00:08:27.821 --> 00:08:29.722
The reason the three of
them aged so quickly

00:08:29.722 --> 00:08:31.324
is because the experiment caused

00:08:31.324 --> 00:08:33.121
a special enzyme to be
produced in their bloodstreams

00:08:33.159 --> 00:08:35.286
that caused sudden damage
to their DNA structures.

00:08:35.395 --> 00:08:38.364
But Kirchner's electrical discharge

00:08:38.364 --> 00:08:39.866
is the result of those enzymes

00:08:39.866 --> 00:08:41.501
and something in his
particular physical make-up...

00:08:41.501 --> 00:08:43.696
I'm sure that you're aware,

00:08:43.937 --> 00:08:46.973
that we must have what you
named the Ged Dimension,

00:08:46.973 --> 00:08:51.010
succeed at being accurately
demonstrated and navigated.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:55.114
The extensive code that was extracted
using x-rays from that piece of stone

00:08:55.114 --> 00:08:57.981
found more than 100 years ago.

00:08:58.551 --> 00:09:01.281
Although many scientists
have researched it,

00:09:01.321 --> 00:09:03.790
it had always remained a mystery.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.359
But, Professor Gherta,
thanks to your efforts,

00:09:06.359 --> 00:09:09.295
that code was revealed to be the plans

00:09:09.295 --> 00:09:11.898
for a machine that opens space and time.

00:09:11.898 --> 00:09:14.300
Furthermore, the results of the latest tests

00:09:14.300 --> 00:09:16.598
have proven that it works.

00:09:17.470 --> 00:09:19.606
The deaths of two of the pilots,

00:09:19.606 --> 00:09:23.276
and the rapid aging of the
three pilots who returned alive,

00:09:23.276 --> 00:09:25.712
are some of the problems we've had but...

00:09:25.712 --> 00:09:27.981
lf, in accordance with the
multidimensional theory

00:09:27.981 --> 00:09:29.816
that is your field of
research, Professor Gherta,

00:09:29.816 --> 00:09:31.217
the Ged Dimension,

00:09:31.217 --> 00:09:34.709
basically the world after
death, is proven to exist,

00:09:34.754 --> 00:09:38.315
it could cause unimaginable
turmoil all over the world.

00:09:38.625 --> 00:09:44.898
Politics, religion, science, and even
military tactics would be affected.

00:09:44.898 --> 00:09:47.100
But at the same time,

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:49.864
it would also become a
source of tremendous profits.

00:09:49.903 --> 00:09:52.171
Before other countries find out about this,

00:09:52.171 --> 00:09:55.742
our country, which is behind
other developed nations,

00:09:55.742 --> 00:09:57.510
wants to present this as
state-of-the-art technology

00:09:57.510 --> 00:09:58.875
developed and researched here.

00:09:58.945 --> 00:10:00.747
That is what His Majesty the King...

00:10:00.747 --> 00:10:03.375
Yes, those are the King's wishes.

00:10:11.791 --> 00:10:15.659
Oh, Demian, we didn't
know you were here.

00:10:15.695 --> 00:10:19.933
That's right, Professor Gherta,
you've never met before, have you?

00:10:19.933 --> 00:10:22.201
This is Demian from the
Royal Security Agency.

00:10:22.201 --> 00:10:25.068
He's a close friend of the prince.

00:10:27.874 --> 00:10:30.643
He's the real power behind this project.

00:10:30.643 --> 00:10:33.669
Yes, I have heard of him.

00:10:34.614 --> 00:10:39.052
I'm sure you've only heard nonsense
about me from these old men,

00:10:39.052 --> 00:10:40.586
Professor Gherta.

00:10:40.586 --> 00:10:43.656
No, without your recommendation

00:10:43.656 --> 00:10:45.925
this very expensive project

00:10:45.925 --> 00:10:49.122
would never have proceeded
as quickly as it has.

00:10:55.101 --> 00:10:57.535
As a scientist, I'm grateful to you.

00:11:19.292 --> 00:11:22.028
Damn it! The M-theory
constant doesn't work either!

00:11:22.028 --> 00:11:23.763
What about Klein's universal law?

00:11:23.763 --> 00:11:25.898
There's also the Scola variable integer.

00:11:25.898 --> 00:11:27.593
How many are there?!

00:11:32.405 --> 00:11:35.670
That's all I can get from
Professor Gherta's documents.

00:11:38.845 --> 00:11:40.403
Where are you going, Cooks?!

00:11:41.848 --> 00:11:43.282
What do you think you're doing?!

00:11:43.282 --> 00:11:45.551
Breaking and entering is bad, Cooks!

00:11:45.551 --> 00:11:47.520
I'm looking for something!

00:11:47.520 --> 00:11:50.656
A police officer doing this kind of
thing could get in serious trouble!

00:11:50.656 --> 00:11:52.291
Forget that! Search!

00:11:52.291 --> 00:11:54.418
Just find anything suspicious!

00:12:04.570 --> 00:12:09.064
Geez! This is a woman's private
bedroom! Under no circumstances...

00:12:14.414 --> 00:12:16.848
Who is this person?

00:12:16.983 --> 00:12:21.215
Conrad Rugen. The man
who discovered x-rays.

00:12:21.287 --> 00:12:24.290
Even all the books have to do with Rugen.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:27.693
His biography, theses,
memoirs and research papers.

00:12:27.693 --> 00:12:31.364
Well, I suppose he was a
highly regarded physicist but...

00:12:31.364 --> 00:12:34.267
Cooks, let's leave! Quickly!

00:12:34.267 --> 00:12:35.468
What's wrong?

00:12:35.468 --> 00:12:37.770
Other people shouldn't come in here.

00:12:37.770 --> 00:12:40.034
This place is very special to Gherta.

00:12:40.540 --> 00:12:42.633
Very special?

00:12:45.545 --> 00:12:47.172
So, that's it.

00:13:03.162 --> 00:13:05.357
Professor Gherta.

00:13:44.937 --> 00:13:48.031
One, eight, four, five, three, two, seven...

00:13:48.374 --> 00:13:50.774
Conrad Rugen's date of birth.

00:13:53.980 --> 00:13:55.615
It opened!

00:13:55.615 --> 00:13:58.448
After all, even scientists are human.

00:14:15.568 --> 00:14:18.366
-Woah!
-What is this place?

00:14:20.273 --> 00:14:22.969
This tunnel is huge.

00:14:46.332 --> 00:14:49.602
Well then, I have a question
for you, as a scientist.

00:14:49.602 --> 00:14:52.002
When will the next test be?

00:14:56.275 --> 00:14:59.073
What's the matter, Professor Gherta?

00:15:01.247 --> 00:15:03.082
However, Demian,

00:15:03.082 --> 00:15:05.451
even though you're from
the Royal Security Agency,

00:15:05.451 --> 00:15:09.422
the schedule for the next test
is decided by this committee.

00:15:09.422 --> 00:15:14.257
We must carefully examine the
experimental data and its objective.

00:15:15.895 --> 00:15:20.833
We must be absolutely certain that
the experiment will be a success.

00:15:20.833 --> 00:15:23.569
If something like what happened
last time should happen again,

00:15:23.569 --> 00:15:26.163
it will be the responsibility
of this committee.

00:15:26.772 --> 00:15:28.908
You may be a friend of the royal family,

00:15:28.908 --> 00:15:30.843
but you can't just ignore the
members of this committee

00:15:30.843 --> 00:15:32.834
and hasten things along.

00:15:43.256 --> 00:15:46.325
You talk too much, old man.

00:15:46.325 --> 00:15:48.316
Professor Gherta.

00:15:50.863 --> 00:15:55.732
How much longer will it take to
complete the Kuril Island Ring?

00:15:56.736 --> 00:15:59.739
It's already been three
years since that accident.

00:15:59.739 --> 00:16:03.609
Worrying about minor details
only creates unnecessary delay,

00:16:03.609 --> 00:16:06.373
even His Majesty the King is concerned.

00:16:19.158 --> 00:16:20.860
I get it.

00:16:20.860 --> 00:16:25.126
That entrance was only used
by Gherta to get in here.

00:16:26.532 --> 00:16:28.701
What do you think they were doing?

00:16:28.701 --> 00:16:30.692
I don't know.

00:16:31.003 --> 00:16:34.837
From the size of it, this place must
spread out under the whole island.

00:16:39.545 --> 00:16:41.380
An underground hospital.

00:16:41.380 --> 00:16:43.712
Look, Cooks!

00:16:44.150 --> 00:16:45.951
This is...

00:16:45.951 --> 00:16:48.511
Grass's family!

00:16:56.796 --> 00:17:00.425
Cooks! This was in the room next door!

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:02.968
Kirchner...

00:17:02.968 --> 00:17:05.338
The man who took a hostage in Clairmont.

00:17:05.338 --> 00:17:07.473
It's probably the same man.

00:17:07.473 --> 00:17:10.509
Though I don't know how he got so old.

00:17:10.509 --> 00:17:13.713
But it's probably the reason
why Gherta and her men

00:17:13.713 --> 00:17:15.781
were so desperately chasing him.

00:17:15.781 --> 00:17:18.217
They were all underground here.

00:17:18.217 --> 00:17:20.685
And then they ran away.

00:17:29.128 --> 00:17:31.562
I guess we can't go any farther.

00:17:53.619 --> 00:17:56.422
C-Could this be?

00:17:56.422 --> 00:17:58.891
The code from the Fragment!

00:17:58.891 --> 00:18:00.882
Then the Ged Group is...

00:18:05.064 --> 00:18:06.588
Cooks!

00:18:11.003 --> 00:18:12.605
Helga?

00:18:12.605 --> 00:18:15.875
Oh, she was transferred to
Chikao on the Natsuna Islands.

00:18:15.875 --> 00:18:17.743
She was a strange girl,

00:18:17.743 --> 00:18:20.837
and the director had a
lot of trouble with her.

00:18:24.183 --> 00:18:28.017
I came here for Cybele's sake.

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.749
She needs me!

00:18:33.893 --> 00:18:38.762
Big Brother? Big Brother! Where are you?!

00:18:40.299 --> 00:18:43.496
Big Brother! Big Brother!

00:18:47.506 --> 00:18:50.134
Big Brother, where are you going?

00:18:50.976 --> 00:18:52.944
Bel.

00:18:57.883 --> 00:19:02.321
It's okay. You don't have to worry, Bel.

00:19:02.321 --> 00:19:05.916
Big Brother has something he has to do.

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:11.186
You're a good girl, Bel,
so I know you'll understand.

00:19:14.400 --> 00:19:17.130
No! No! No!

00:19:19.271 --> 00:19:21.432
Here, Bel.

00:19:34.487 --> 00:19:36.216
Come on, Bel.

00:19:42.228 --> 00:19:52.229
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea

00:19:53.539 --> 00:20:03.278
A small flower is resting

00:20:03.782 --> 00:20:13.282
The melody of a gentle wind
passes through a rainbow

00:20:14.093 --> 00:20:22.467
Playing in the sky

00:20:22.968 --> 00:20:27.735
Everyone plays the music of love

00:20:27.873 --> 00:20:32.845
A warm light came down

00:20:32.845 --> 00:20:41.480
(A gaze) That gaze is
unbound and becomes full

00:20:41.954 --> 00:20:47.256
Embraced by water

00:20:54.967 --> 00:20:57.333
It's Chikao.

00:21:11.116 --> 00:21:13.676
Chitto. Chitto.

00:21:15.688 --> 00:21:17.690
H-Helga?

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:19.157
Let's go.

00:21:19.391 --> 00:21:20.881
Yeah.

00:22:35.567 --> 00:22:45.374
At the bottom of the deep, clear sea
fukaku fukaku sukitooru umi no soko ni

00:22:45.644 --> 00:22:55.487
A small flower is resting
chiisana hana madoronderu

00:22:55.487 --> 00:23:00.220
The melody of a gentle wind
amayaka na kaze no shirabe

00:23:00.259 --> 00:23:05.094
Passes through a rainbow
niji wo kuguri

00:23:05.497 --> 00:23:14.633
The fish are playing in the sky
sakanatachi wa sora ni asobu

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:19.812
Everyone plays the music of love
dare mo ga ai wo kanaderu

00:23:19.812 --> 00:23:25.084
A warm light came down
atatakana hikari futteta

00:23:25.084 --> 00:23:29.487
(A gaze) That gaze
(manazashi wa) sono manazashi wa

00:23:29.521 --> 00:23:33.826
Is unbound and becomes full
hodokete michiteku

00:23:33.826 --> 00:23:38.695
Embraced by water
mizu ni dakare
